Bugfix: Stop the code integrity check from warning about an unsigned distribution

A fresh installation from a release archive showed "There were problems with the
code integrity check" and listed core plus every shipped app with
MissingSignatureException, "Signature data not found." Nothing an administrator
could do made it go away.

ownCloud.online does not sign its releases: there is no signature package and no
certificate to verify against, so the check could never pass. The repository
already declares the unsigned channel 'bwtech', but the release build rewrites
version.php to 'stable', which turned the check back on for exactly the artefacts
that ship to customers. Switching the update channel in the admin panel had the
same effect, so channel alone is not a sound criterion.

Enforcement now additionally requires core/signature.json to exist. An unsigned
distribution reports nothing, and the day a signed one is built the check turns
itself back on. A distribution that does carry signatures is unaffected.

